promised a scoring of an incomplete share file under stamped names, and on a file
holding only the lens arm, which is what decompose.py --quick writes, the script
named the missing control arms in its log and then stopped with a KeyError at its
line 245 before writing any of the four outputs; a file holding two of the twelve
layers failed the same way at line 356. The script now refuses only what it cannot
diagnose at all, which is a file with no lens arm or a lens arm missing a state
family, and otherwise computes what the input supports and records every reading
it could not compute by name, in this log, in the stamped verdict file under
input_completeness.not_computed, and at the top of the tables. Verified on two
partial shapes built in the scratchpad from the committed shares: the lens-only
copy and a two-layer copy both produce all four stamped diagnostic outputs and
name what is missing. Second, the figure was redrawn to carry what specification
section 7.5 item 1 asks for, the per-layer share curves of every family and every
control at all twelve layers. It has six panels: one per dictionary arm across the
top, each with all seven families, and the two single-state panels and the
against-chance panel across the bottom. Effect on the record: every value that
existed in the previous verdicts.json is unchanged, a leaf-by-leaf comparison of
